/T (In the wake of the tragic shooting at Utah Valley University, our county has been reminded of both the fragility of life and the strength that comes when we stand together. In response, mayors from across Utah County joined together to release a unified statement.  In it, we affirmed our commitment to accountability, compassion, caring for one another, and to the shared belief that we are stronger together and that healing comes when we support one another as neighbors.)
/E (In the wake of the tragic shooting at Utah Valley University, our county has been reminded of both the fragility of life and the strength that comes when we stand together. In response, mayors from across Utah County joined together to release a unified statement.  In it, we affirmed our commitment to accountability, compassion, caring for one another, and to the shared belief that we are stronger together and that healing comes when we support one another as neighbors.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (MESSAGE FROM THE MAYOR)
/E (MESSAGE FROM THE MAYOR)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (These kinds of moments test us. They bring to the surface the reality that we live in a world that often feels divided, whether by politics, opinion, or circumstance. But tragedy also reveals something else: that beneath our differences lies a deep, human need to belong and to feel connected. We must disagree. These shared perspectives are what has built our community and keeps us thriving. Unity does not erase our individuality, but it does bind us together in our shared humanity, a reminder as to the purpose and reason for our civil discourse. When we choose to stand shoulder to shoulder, we send a powerful message, that darkness will not define us and that, together, we can create light.)
/E (These kinds of moments test us. They bring to the surface the reality that we live in a world that often feels divided, whether by politics, opinion, or circumstance. But tragedy also reveals something else: that beneath our differences lies a deep, human need to belong and to feel connected. We must disagree. These shared perspectives are what has built our community and keeps us thriving. Unity does not erase our individuality, but it does bind us together in our shared humanity, a reminder as to the purpose and reason for our civil discourse. When we choose to stand shoulder to shoulder, we send a powerful message, that darkness will not define us and that, together, we can create light.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Here in Vineyard, we have an opportunity to reflect that light in meaningful ways. In the days following the hurt our community faced, we came together in reflection, we came together in gratitude for the kindness of those who give their lives for us, and 400+ of us came together to serve the community, showing up for Vineyard. We can continue to show up.)
/E (Here in Vineyard, we have an opportunity to reflect that light in meaningful ways. In the days following the hurt our community faced, we came together in reflection, we came together in gratitude for the kindness of those who give their lives for us, and 400+ of us came together to serve the community, showing up for Vineyard. We can continue to show up.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
